---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout title="About the studio" description="Studio No Frame is a Berlin studio for exhibition architecture, art production, project management and curation, led by Yelta Köm. Partners include HKW, Pera Museum, SALT, Museum Ludwig and the Venice and Istanbul biennials.">
  <section class="page">
    <span class="label">About</span>
    <h1>A studio that takes the shape of the work it houses.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Studio No Frame is a Berlin-based studio working across art direction,
        exhibition design, art production, project management, curation and
        consulting. We work with artists, cultural institutions, NGOs, project
        spaces and universities on interdisciplinary and socially engaged
        projects.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our structure is flexible and our team is mixed by design. Each project
        starts from its own material: the works, the building, the people who
        will move through it. We value collective thinking, experimental
        methods and process-oriented making, and we plan production so that
        material and budget are spent where visitors actually feel them.
      </p>

      <h2>Partners</h2>
      <p>
        Haus der Kulturen der Welt, Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts
        (İKSV), Istanbul Modern, Museum Ludwig, MAXXI Rome, Pera Museum, SALT,
        La Biennale di Venezia, the Istanbul Biennial, the Istanbul Design
        Biennial and the Timișoara Biennial. Artists we have worked with
        include Abbas Zahedi, Ahmet Öğüt, Amy Lien &amp; Enzo Camacho, Ayşe
        Erkmen, Füsun Onur, Gülsün Karamustafa, Leman Darıcıoğlu, Monira Al
        Qadiri, Raul Walch and Tomás Saraceno.
      </p>

      <h2>Team</h2>
      <p>
        The studio is led by <strong>Yelta Köm</strong>, an Istanbul-born
        architect and artist who has lived and worked in Berlin for over a
        decade. His practice centres on spatial interventions and temporary
        setups built with institutions, artists and communities.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work with a rotating group of designers, researchers and production
        managers, and we bring in collaborators to suit each exhibition rather
        than fitting every show to a fixed team.
      </p>

      <h2>Working with us</h2>
      <p>
        To see the full portfolio or discuss a project,
        <a href={`${base}/contact`}>get in touch</a>. If you are looking for an
        internship, the details are on the
        <a href={`${base}/internships`}>internships page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
